# ELLAN LAB — order_pickup_service migration

## Context
Decomposing OPS monolith (15k lines, Python/FastAPI) into microservices using Strangler Fig + DDD + Event-Driven.
Stack: FastAPI · SQLAlchemy async · PostgreSQL · Redis Streams/Kafka · Pydantic v2 · pytest.

## Ownership rules (never violate)
- OPS = orchestrator only. Never persist catalog/partner/wallet/inventory data as master.
- catalog-service = owner of SKU/price/attributes.
- inventory-service = owner of physical stock per locker.
- partner-service = owner of partner CRUD + webhooks.
- wallet-service = owner of credits/wallet.
- notification-service = owner of delivery (OPS only enqueues).
- logistics-service = owner of manifest/SLA.

## Current state
- Done (90-100%): catalog, inventory, notification, wallet, logistics services in 01_source/.
- In progress (45%): partner-service.
- Pending in OPS monolith: HTTP routing to new services, removal of legacy routers.

## Feature flags in OPS (app/core/config.py)
USE_CATALOG_SERVICE · USE_PARTNER_SERVICE · USE_INVENTORY_SERVICE
USE_WALLET_SERVICE · USE_LOGISTICS_SERVICE · SHADOW_MODE_ENABLED

## Mandatory patterns
1. Shadow mode BEFORE enabling any feature flag.
2. Every new service needs GET /health/ready + GET /health/live.
3. All Kafka consumers need idempotency + DLQ.
4. Inventory reservations use optimistic locking.
5. DB table prefix: catalog_, partner_, inventory_, wallet_.
6. Rollback = feature flag flip < 1 min. Trigger: error rate > 0.5% / 5 min.

## When generating code
- Reference file paths (01_source/...) instead of repeating full implementations.
- Check existing service in 01_source/ before creating new files.
- Follow the DTO contract OrderPickupProductCacheDTO (never change fields without versioning).
- Write pytest tests for all new services matching inventory_service test coverage pattern.

## Anti-patterns — NEVER do
- OPS owning product/partner/credit data as source of truth.
- Removing monolith code without feature flag + stable canary.
- New service without health probes.
- Kafka consumer without DLQ.
